{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Is my father still alive, etc.</b> Even though they had already told him that he was alive, as is clear from all of Judah's words, in any case Joseph thought: perhaps they said this in order to stir up his compassion for the old man, so that he would not cause him death, since his soul is bound up with his soul. Therefore he asked them again, 'Is my father still alive?' — but their heart did not think so, and they thought that he did not intend to ask whether he was alive or not, but rather came to remind them of their sin. Therefore he said, 'Is my father still alive' — to say that he is his father and not their father, for they had not spared his pain as though he were not their father. Therefore they were dismayed and could not answer him a word." "And there is yet another reason for this dismay: because he said 'I am Joseph' and did not mention 'your brother,' therefore they were dismayed, hurried, trembling seized them there, for they said: perhaps he seeks to be an enemy and take vengeance and distance himself from brotherhood, just as they had done to him when they distanced themselves from brotherhood, as Rashi explained on the verse ״נָסְעוּ מִזֶּה״ (Genesis 37:17). Therefore he said to them a second time, 'I am Joseph your brother, whom you sold into Egypt' — even if at the very least you should have sold me to some other nation that is not so steeped in licentiousness, in any case I am your brother, and let it not be grievous in your eyes that you sold me here to Egypt, for Elohim sent me before you for sustenance. For I see that the matter has come about such that I arrived among those steeped in licentiousness, and the incident with the wife of Potiphar befell me, in which I mastered my inclination, and through this I merited to become the shepherd of Israel, their sustainer and provider, as it is written (Genesis 49:24) ״וַיֵּשֶׁב בְּאֵיתָן קַשְׁתּוֹ וְגוֹ׳ מִשָּׁם רֹעֶה אֶבֶן יִשְׂרָאֵל״. And our Rabbis of blessed memory agreed with this, for they said (Sotah 4a): 'Anyone who lies with another man's wife ultimately seeks a loaf of bread and does not find it,' etc. And had I not been among those steeped in licentiousness, perhaps another man would have been chosen to remedy the two years of famine; but since it became available to me that I was sold to a people steeped in licentiousness, none of them merited to remedy the famine except me. And if so, this sale here to Egypt is what caused me that Elohim sent me before you for sustenance." "And our Rabbis of blessed memory said (Genesis Rabbah 93:11) that from this dismay a lesson may be drawn regarding the Day of Judgment, as Rabbi Elazar ben Azariah said: 'Woe to us from the Day of Judgment, woe to us from the Day of Reproof.' And if Joseph, when he said to his brothers 'I am Joseph,' they could not answer him — when the Holy One, blessed be He, stands in judgment, how much more so, as it is said (Isaiah 10:3) ״וּמַה תַּעֲשׂוּ לְיוֹם פְּקֻדָּה״ etc. For the brothers thought that Joseph was reminding them of their sin in the manner explained above, and what will a person do on the day of reckoning when his dwelling, his burdens, and his commerce are examined, and in the hand of every person a seal will be pressed to say, 'See your ways — what you have done!' And this is the view of Rabbi Elazar, that the Torah wrote for us that the brothers were dismayed in order that the discerning person will take to heart the terror of the Day of Judgment and draw an a fortiori inference from the brothers of Joseph."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 45, :notes {2 "Genesis Rabbah citation 'צג י' resolved as chapter 93, section 11. In the Isaiah verse and the closing warning, I read 'יַחְתּוֹן לוֹמַר רְאִי דַרְכֵּךְ מֶה עָשִׂית' as a divine summons addressed in the feminine singular (to the soul or congregation), rendered literally without smoothing."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:33:30.985785442Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}